    </prelobbyBriefings>
    <prelobbyNdas>
      <Value><![CDATA[1 | You (hereafter 'the asset') will never say 'risalamande' to a colleague. Call it 'the dessert matter'.
1 | If asked what you scanned, you scanned nothing. It was a menu. You were hungry.
1 | You will not write any of this on a whiteboard, a sticky note or an Azure DevOps ticket, however refined.
1 | Should you find the almond, you will show no emotion. Joy is a tell.
1 | You accept that everyone around you signed something slightly different. Trust no one's version.
1 | This oath expires when the last dessert bowl is cleared, or never, whichever legal prefers.
1 | I swear I have never heard of the risalamande.
2 | The undersigned (hereafter 'the leak') agrees to tell at least three colleagues about this page, vaguely.
2 | You will mention the risalamande at every opportunity, including stand-up, where it is not relevant.
2 | You will get one detail wrong on purpose. Rumours need room to grow.
2 | If you find the almond, you will announce it at once, at full volume. No poker faces.
2 | You will reply all. To everything. Until the julefrokost.
2 | You may discuss The Project on any Azure DevOps board, provided the ticket is assigned to somebody else.
2 | I agree to tell the horses everything.
3 | The undersigned (hereafter 'the stakeholder') confirms the scope is final, for the next few minutes.
3 | Anything you ask for on the night is a change request. Change requests are answered in January.
3 | You will not say 'while you're in there' or 'just one small thing' to anyone holding a phone.
3 | If you find the almond, you will log it as a feature. It was always in the plan.
3 | You accept that your estimate was wrong before you made it, and that you will be held to it anyway.
3 | This agreement replaces all earlier versions of this agreement, including the one you are reading.
3 | I approve this version, and the next two.
4 | The undersigned (hereafter 'the learner') confirms they read every slide and did not just press Next.
4 | You may discuss this module only with colleagues who were also assigned it. Ask around. Compare notes.
4 | You will lift scope with your knees, not your back.
4 | If you find the almond, you will fill in the almond form. There is no almond form. Proceed anyway.
4 | Estimates given during this module are for training purposes only and will be used against you.
4 | You understand that a horse may be present, and that the horse has completed this training.
4 | I confirm I pressed Next without reading.
5 | The undersigned (hereafter 'cc') confirms they attended a meeting they were not invited to.
5 | If asked about the minutes, you will say 'let's take that offline' and never take it offline.
5 | You will not forward this to colleagues. You will describe it badly from memory instead.
5 | Any estimate you nodded at is now your estimate.
5 | If you find the almond, it goes on the agenda. You will present it. Two slides, no more.
5 | You accept that the horses were consulted first, and that their feedback was the more actionable.
5 | I agree this could have been an email.
6 | The undersigned (hereafter 'the tall one') agrees that the nisse was here first and has seniority.
6 | You will not discuss the nisse with colleagues. If they mention a nisse, it is a different nisse.
6 | Estimates are to be left by the server rack overnight. The nisse will halve them.
6 | If you find the almond, you will thank the nisse out loud. It can hear you.
6 | You will not deploy on a Friday without leaving porridge. This is how incidents happen.
6 | The horses know about the nisse. The nisse knows about the horses. You will stay out of it.
6 | I agree to leave the nisse its porridge.
7 | The undersigned (hereafter 'on-call') approves a production change on a Friday evening, in writing.
7 | You will not ask whether it has been tested. It works on our machine.
7 | If a colleague asks what you scanned, you will say 'a status page' and look tired.
7 | If you find the almond, you will not turn it off and on again. Push it out.
7 | All estimates are given in Friday deploys: it takes either a moment or the whole weekend.
7 | The horses were migrated first, as a pilot. They report no issues. They report nothing at all.
7 | I approve deploying on a Friday.
8 | The undersigned (hereafter 'the resource') confirms that this is about timesheets, to anyone who asks.
8 | You will register the evening under 'internal, other, misc, see comment' and leave the comment blank.
8 | You will not discuss The Project with colleagues, except in fifteen-minute increments.
8 | If you find the almond, you will not expense it. It is already a benefit in kind.
8 | Estimates are billed by the hour. Being wrong is billed separately.
8 | You accept that the horses submit their hours on time, every week, and that it has been noticed.
8 | I agree that this was about timesheets.
9 | The undersigned (hereafter 'the angel') invests in a company with no product, no name and no founder.
9 | You will describe this opportunity to colleagues as 'early' and decline to elaborate.
9 | All estimates are forward-looking statements. So is the product. So are you.
9 | If you find the almond, it is a liquidity event. You will stay calm and not ring a bell.
9 | Your shares convert to nothing at midnight. This is known as a party round.
9 | You accept that the horses passed on this deal, and that horses have been wrong before.
9 | I agree that past almonds do not guarantee future almonds.
10 | The undersigned (hereafter 'a factor') agrees that nobody is to blame, least of all the undersigned.
10 | You will not say 'it worked in the pre-lobby' at any point during the incident.
10 | If asked what happened, you will answer with a timeline and no adjectives.
10 | If you find the almond, you will not call it a root cause. It is a finding.
10 | Estimates of time to recovery will be given confidently and revised hourly.
10 | You accept that the horses were on call and did not pick up.
10 | I agree it was nobody's fault, especially not mine.
11 | The undersigned (hereafter 'the name below') agrees to answer to the name below and to nothing else.
11 | You have never met your colleagues. If one greets you, say 'new here' and compliment their jumper.
11 | Your job title is whatever you pick on the night. You will defend it in meetings as if it were real.
11 | If you find the almond, you will take the mandelgave and ask no questions about where it came from.
11 | Your previous estimates belong to your previous identity. Unfortunately, so do the deadlines.
11 | You accept that the horses have also been relocated. You will not look for them.
11 | I agree that I have always been this person.
12 | The undersigned (hereafter 'the candidate') is thrilled to announce absolutely nothing until the night.
12 | You will not update LinkedIn before the final round. 'Founder & CEO (pending)' fools nobody.
12 | If a colleague asks whether you were approached too, say 'I'm happy where I am' and blink twice.
12 | If you find the almond, it does not count as a competing offer.
12 | Your greatest weakness is your estimates. You will say so before we do.
12 | You accept that a horse is also on the shortlist, and that it interviews well.
12 | I agree that I am open to opportunities.
13 | The undersigned (hereafter 'the passenger') will locate the nearest exit. It may be a promotion.
13 | You will keep your phone charged, upright and out of flight mode for the whole evening.
13 | In the event of scope creep, masks will drop. Fit your own before assisting the product owner.
13 | If you find the almond, remain seated until the mandelgave has come to a complete stop.
13 | You will not discuss this briefing with passengers in other rows. Their briefing was different.
13 | Smoking, estimating and horses are not permitted in the lavatories.
13 | I agree that my nearest exit may be behind me.
14 | The undersigned (hereafter 'the user') has read and understood these terms, which makes one of us.
14 | You accept all cookies. The baked kind too. You may not manage your preferences.
14 | You will not tell colleagues what you agreed to. You do not know what you agreed to.
14 | We may update these terms at any time, including during this sentence, which now mentions the almond.
14 | If you find the almond, it is yours, subject to clauses we have not written yet.
14 | Estimates are provided 'as is', without warranty of any kind, express or implied.
14 | I agree to whatever this was.]]></Value>
    </prelobbyNdas>
